    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "My current research is directed towards understanding the interaction between fracture mechanics, fluid flow, and the processes that form the altered zones. Specifically I would like to answer the following questions:\r\n1) How does the formation of the chemically altered zone affect the development of opening modes joints?\r\na) Can changes in heat and volume associated with chemical reactions act as a driving force for fracture propagation?\r\nb) What factors control the spatial distribution of mineral zoning adjacent to a fracture in porous sandstone?\r\nc) How does the chemical and physical inhomogeneity associated with zoning affect fracture propagation?\r\n2)What can we learn about the nature and history of fluid flow through the host rock system from the chemically altered region associated with the fracture?",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
